[tool_use] Agent {"description":"Code review Phase 4","subagent_type":"code-reviewer","prompt":"Review Phase 4 changes for correctness, architecture, DRY, drift, and test sufficiency per `/home/aaron/dev/projects/aaron/pointfight-reactor/docs/QUALITY_GATES.md`.\n\nPhase context: 1 = local MVP; 2 = rounds + configurable input + motion + penalty; 3 = visuospatial cues + distance axis + audio; 4 adds drill-profile CRUD, an explicit `lateThresholdMs` band distinct from `responseWindowMs`, per-profile cue subset (`allowedCueIds`), configurable `scoreWeights`, a per-cue summary breakdown, and an anti-rhythm narrative.\n\nFiles in scope (changes since the last `phase-3:` commit `4b94ff6`):\n- `app/src/engine/types.ts` (new DrillConfig fields: lateThresholdMs, allowedCueIds, scoreWeights; new DEFAULT_SCORE_WEIGHTS; SCORE_TABLE removed; SettingsRecord gains activeProfileId?)\n- `app/src/engine/drill.ts` (classifyRep + classifyPreCuePress now take scoreWeights; classifyRep splits hesitation/late at lateThresholdMs; pickNextCue filters by allowedCueIds; validateDrillConfig adds threshold-ordering + cue-subset rules; NEW cueBreakdown + antiRhythmSignal pure helpers)\n- `app/src/engine/drill.test.ts` (refactored classifyRep tests to use a `cls()` builder; added late-threshold boundary tests, cue subset tests, validateDrillConfig threshold/subset tests, cueBreakdown tests, antiRhythmSignal tests, classifyPreCuePress weight test)\n- `app/src/cues/library.ts` (unchanged)\n- `app/src/store/db.ts` (Dexie schema bumped to v3 with profiles table)\n- `app/src/store/profiles.ts` (NEW — ProfileRecord, listProfiles/getProfile/saveProfile/deleteProfile/ensureAtLeastOneProfile/buildDefaultProfile)\n- `app/src/store/profiles.test.ts` (NEW — CRUD + ensure idempotency + setActiveProfile)\n- `app/src/store/settings-types.ts` (activeProfileId?)\n- `app/src/store/settings.ts` (loadActiveProfile that migrates Phase 2/3 settings into a seeded Default profile on first run; setActiveProfile)\n- `app/src/store/session.ts` (passes scoreWeights + lateThresholdMs into classifyRep / classifyPreCuePress)\n- `app/src/ui/SettingsScreen.tsx` (full rewrite — profile picker + create/rename/delete + per-profile editor across Rounds / Pre-cue delay / Choice-RT thresholds / Cue subset / Scoring weights / Visuals / Penalty)\n- `app/src/ui/IdleScreen.tsx` (loads active profile + passes profile.config to start())\n- `app/src/ui/SummaryScreen.tsx` (per-cue breakdown table; rhythm panel using antiRhythmSignal narrative; Start-another now passes config + inputSource through)\n- `app/src/App.css` (new styles for profile-actions, cue-subset-grid, score-grid, rhythm-panel)\n- `artifacts/decision-memo.md` (rewritten for Phase 4)\n\nVerified locally: lint clean; typecheck clean; 79/79 tests pass; build succeeds.\n\nSpecifically check:\n- DRY: the rule for distinguishing late from hesitation is now in classifyRep; is there any duplication elsewhere (e.g. in summarize / cueBreakdown) that could rot independently?\n- Drift: Phase 2/3 SettingsRecord still carries the drill fields used as migration seeds. Is the migration in loadActiveProfile correct for users who already have Phase 2/3 data? Are old sessions still listed correctly on the idle screen?\n- Tests: do new tests cover every new public behavior (classifyRep late boundary, allowedCueIds, scoreWeights, cueBreakdown, antiRhythmSignal, profiles CRUD, loadActiveProfile migration)?\n- Architecture: profiles module isolated from engine? Engine helpers still pure? Migration idempotent across reloads?\n- Correctness risks: profile delete must keep at least one profile; SettingsScreen handles that. Cue subset validation must reject zero go cues when distance axis off. Threshold ordering enforced.\n\nReport APPROVE / REQUEST_CHANGES with file:line findings. Under 400 words.","run_in_background":true}
