[text] Phase 4 of PointFight Reactor needs browser verification. Dev server runs at http://localhost:5177/.

Verify the six Phase 4 acceptance criteria plus a Phase 3 regression. Phase 4 adds:
- drill-profile CRUD (Settings → Profile → Active profile dropdown + New / Rename / Delete buttons)
- a new "Choice-RT thresholds" section in Settings (hesitation / late / response-window) with default hesitation=450, late=600, responseWindow=1200
- a "Cue subset" section (8 cue checkboxes) — must keep at least one go cue
- a "Scoring weights" section (5 numeric inputs)
- the Summary screen now shows a per-cue breakdown table (cue, reps, correct, FS, hes, late, avg RT, best-10 RT)
- the Summary screen now shows a Rhythm pattern panel with a narrative ("No rhythm pattern detected." or "False starts most often after ..." )

C1 — Profile CRUD
- Open Settings. Confirm the Profile section has an Active profile dropdown (default seeded as "Default") and New / Rename / Delete buttons.
- Click New profile → name it "Sparring". Verify the dropdown now includes "Sparring" and it is the active profile.
- Click Rename → rename to "Sparring v2". Verify dropdown updates.
- Click Delete with confirmation. Verify the dropdown drops back to "Default".
- With only "Default" left, Delete should show an error banner saying "Cannot delete the only remaining profile.".

C2 — Per-profile configurability
- Switch back to a fresh Sparring profile. Change rounds=2, work=3s, rest=2s, hesitation=400, late=700, response-window=1500, distance axis ON. Save.
- Re-open Settings, switch to Default, then back to Sparring — values should round-trip.

C3 — Hesitation/Late thresholds in action
- With Sparring active (hesitation=400, late=700), start a drill. Fire one fast rep (< 400ms ideally), one slow rep that should be a hesitation (~500ms via timing), and one very slow (~750ms) that should classify as late despite being inside the response window. Hard to time exactly; use 0-rep + finishWindow path by NOT pressing → that should be late.
- Verify the late feedback colour (warn) appears for at least one rep. Verify the summary screen counts the late.

C4 — Cue subset
- Settings → Cue subset → uncheck all go cues except "STEPS IN". Save. Start drill (Sparring). Run several reps without pressing. Confirm only `steps_in` (and any kept no-go cues) appear. Use the SVG class name `.cue-steps-in` to verify.
- Try unchecking all go cues. Save should show a validation error banner mentioning "at least one go cue".

C5 — Per-cue summary breakdown
- Run a short drill against Default (with all cues allowed) for ~30 reps mixing presses and no-presses. End the drill (Esc). On the summary screen, the new table should show at least 3 different cue rows with reps/correct/FS/hes/late/avg-RT/best-10-RT columns populated. Screenshot.

C6 — Anti-rhythm narrative
- During the same summary screen, the "Rhythm pattern" panel should display either "No rhythm pattern detected." or a "False starts most often..." sentence. Verify the panel is present and non-empty.

Phase 3 regression
- With all toggles default, distance axis off, run a normal drill. Verify SVG cue pictographs still render and the work/rest cycle still works.

Report PASS / FAIL per criterion. Save screenshots under `artifacts/phase4-verify/`. Track console errors (zero is the expected baseline). Under 500 words.
